{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3N9bzaHZ7ZerSGj5Az","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ligand-field fit for LiGa₅O₈:Ni²⁺ (octahedral d⁸, ³A₂g ground state):\n\n**1. Dq from the lowest band.** For d⁸, the lowest spin-allowed band ³A₂g → ³T₂g sits at exactly 10Dq. So 10Dq = 9 770 cm⁻¹ and **Dq = 977 cm⁻¹**.\n\n**2. B from the two ³T₁g bands.** The ³T₁g(F) and ³T₁g(P) levels mix with each other. Their energies are E = 7.5B + 15Dq ∓ ½√(225B² − 180B·Dq + 100Dq²). Adding the two gives ν₂ + ν₃ = 15B + 30Dq, so:\n- B = (ν₂ + ν₃ − 3ν₁)/15 = (16 050 + 26 740 − 29 310)/15\n- **B ≈ 899 cm⁻¹**\n\nCheck: putting Dq = 977 and B = 899 back in gives ν₂ = 15 938 cm⁻¹ and ν₃ = 26 853 cm⁻¹. The observed values are 16 050 and 26 740 cm⁻¹, so each is off by about 110 cm⁻¹.\n\nThe two bands do not quite agree on B when taken separately. ν₂ alone needs B ≈ 950 cm⁻¹ and ν₃ alone needs B ≈ 890 cm⁻¹. A free least-squares fit of all three triplet bands, which also lets Dq move, gives Dq ≈ 983 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 883 cm⁻¹ (RMS error about 50 cm⁻¹). The uncertainty in B is therefore roughly ±20–50 cm⁻¹.\n\n**3. C from the spin-forbidden ¹E band.** The triplet bands do not depend on C, so only the ¹Eg(D) band can fix it. I computed the full d⁸ energy matrix at Dq = 977 and B = 899 cm⁻¹:\n- At C = 3 000 cm⁻¹, ¹Eg(a) lies at 12 726 cm⁻¹.\n- At C = 3 500 cm⁻¹, it lies at 13 726 cm⁻¹.\n- So ¹E rises by exactly 2 cm⁻¹ for each 1 cm⁻¹ increase in C.\n\nMatching the observed 12 987 cm⁻¹ gives C = 3 000 + (12 987 − 12 726)/2 ≈ **3 130 cm⁻¹**, so C/B ≈ 3.5. This C depends on the B chosen above.\n\n**Result:** Dq ≈ 977 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 899 cm⁻¹, C ≈ 3 130 cm⁻¹. These give 10Dq/B ≈ 10.9.\n\n{\"Dq\": 977, \"B\": 899, \"C\": 3130, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq from nu1, B from nu2+nu3 = 15B+30Dq, C fitted to the 1E band via the d8 energy matrix.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{